  × This sort comparator returns a boolean instead of a number.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ array.sort((a, b) => a > b);
      │            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ [].sort((a, b) => a > b);
    4 │ Array.from(iterable).sort((a, b) => a > b);
  
  i The sort method treats true as 1 and false as 0, so the comparator can never put the first item before the second. The items aren't sorted correctly, and the result can differ between JavaScript engines.
  
  i Return a negative number, zero, or a positive number instead, such as a - b for numbers or a.localeCompare(b) for strings.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Subtract the compared values instead.
  
      1   1 │   /* should generate diagnostics */
